// "Scry N" [CR#701.22a]: look at the top N cards of your library, then put any
// number of them on the bottom of your library in any order and the rest on
// top in any order. "Your" is the actor's. The look reads its slice back by
// identity, so its number is N's: "that card" for scry 1, "those cards" for
// scry 2 (`lookAndSortSlice`). Scry 0 makes no scry event [CR#701.22b],
// which is the rules' to apply, as connive 0's is (`conniveN`).
KeywordAction(
    name: "scry",
    params: [Amount],
    spelling: "scry <Param(0)>",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "scry",
        third_person: "scries",
        frame_set: Custom(frames: [[], [Amount], [ObjectNounPhrase]]),
    ),
    body: lookAndSortSlice(slice(Top, Param(0), library(actor)), onBottom, [Placement(InOrder(AnyOrder))]),
)
